3 at true master (a717da28 lineage) is GREEN on all three lanes: JVM 4,887 tests / 303,186 assertions / 0 failures (the 3 latte items are the yang.clojure track's recorded BLOCKED gate, pre-existing); Dart cljd 4,508 / 0; Node cljs 4,608 / 158,495 / 0 failures. The earlier failure reports all traced to the stale-clone base (fixed, codified a717da28). (2) generators-v1: ALREADY ACTIVE at master — completed-steps carries :p4-s8 and the generator fixtures ran green inside the G3 consumer namespaces; kimi's checkpoint-B authorization was thus already exercised; no round needed. (3) The delegate-tooling corrections, owner-prompted: agy argon is quota-walled (~161h) but agy's OTHER models are live (claude-opus-5-5-high and gemini-3.8-flash-high probed real responses) — model-level routing recorded; my two flips on agy availability (out -> in -> intermittently-out -> model-level) both traced to trusting session-level errors over fresh probes. muse on shiva WORKS: the earlier \"cannot sandbox\" read was wrong — the headless invocation needed --trust-workspace (interactive muse trusts by itself; the owner verified by running muse interactively in ~/workspace/datomworld). The delegate-reference gains the flag in the muse recipe (ca6dd750, pushed). (4) The xlang slice-1 round (the shared conformance helper + the TS<->PHP legs, the postwalk rewrites deleted) runs on muse with --trust-workspace: cross_lang_test.clj +31/-136 in progress.\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:721:Next: muse returns -> the shiva gate on feat/xlang-matrix -> the kimi quality review -> land slice 1 -> dispatch slice 2 (python + yang.clojure legs, the full 4-frontend matrix); then the P7-a budget round and the P4 S9-S12 / P6 S6+ steps.\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:725:Done: (1) The cross_lang rebuild is COMPLETE on master. Slice 1 (kimi, e5888d91, merged 716326aa): test/yang/call/conformance.clj (the shared helper: donors published