r key, so\n+   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n+  [node]\n+  (let [tag (:type node)\n+        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n+    (when-not slots\n+      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n+    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n+                           (case kind\n+                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n+                             :nodes (update n field\n+                                            (fn [children]\n+                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n+                                                    children)))\n+                             n))\n+                         node\n+                         slots)]\n+      (cond-> walked\n+        (= :application tag) (assoc :yang/call-site 1)))))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\nindex 35db43c1..2668cb67 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n@@ -39,6 +39,20 @@\n    :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n \n \n+(defn clojure-manifest\n+  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n+   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n+   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n+   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n+   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n+   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n+   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n+  []\n+  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n+         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n+         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n+\n+\n (defn- clojure-lower\n   [forms]\n   (if (= 1 (count forms))\n@@ -78,7 +92,7 @@\n    returns.\"\n   []\n   (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n-    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n+    true (frontend/install (clojure-manifest)\n                            {:input :forms,\n                             :parse identity,\n                             :lower clojure-lower})\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\nindex b0d222ca..1bb7ca84 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\n@@ -1609,6 +1609,20 @@\n                (into tuples (map (fn [[path id]] [root path id]) frontier)))))))\n \n \n+(defn application-occurrences\n+  \"The `[root path]` of every `:application` occurrence of the projected\n+   row set `tree`: the occurrence relation joined on the row tags, with\n+   no origin — a composition fixes the origin from its own side, as with\n+   `occurrences`. This is the eligible-site derivation of the call-site\n+   occurrence contract: one pair per place, so a shared application row\n+   at two places counts twice.\"\n+  [{:keys [rows] :as tree}]\n+  (into #{}\n+        (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]] (= :application (nth (get rows id) 1))))\n+              (map (fn [[root path _]] [root path])))\n+        (occurrences tree)))\n+\n+\n (def occurrence-rules\n   \"§4.5/§7.7: root-scoped occurrence rules, as portable data. A name is\n    bound at `[root path]` iff a `:lambda` occurrence of the same root sits\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\nindex 1bda6def..acbbf2f7 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\n@@ -227,35 +227,122 @@\n                               {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n \n \n+(def ^:private call-site-key\n+  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\n+   contract C1 (`yang.clojure`), enforced at this boundary but not\n+   owned by it.\"\n+  :yang/call-site)\n+\n+\n+(defn- marked-call-sites\n+  \"The `[path value]` of every node of map AST `ast` carrying the C1\n+   key, walked by the row grammar. Literal payloads are data, never\n+   syntax, and are not walked. Member ASTs are already projected by the\n+   time this runs, so every tag is a grammar tag.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (letfn [(walk\n+            [node path]\n+            (into (if (contains? node call-site-key)\n+                    [[path (get node call-site-key)]]\n+                    [])\n+                  (mapcat (fn [[j [field kind]]]\n+                            (let [pos (+ j 2)\n+                                  value (get node field)]\n+                              (case kind\n+                                :node (walk value (conj path pos))\n+                                :nodes (mapcat (fn [[i child]]\n+                                                 (walk child\n+                                                       (conj path [pos i])))\n+                                               (map-indexed vector value))\n+                                nil)))\n+                          (map-indexed vector\n+                                       (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n+                                            (:type node))))))]\n+    (walk ast [])))\n+\n+\n+(defn- check-call-site-claim!\n+  \"Refuse a batch member whose C1 markers do not exactly cover its\n+   projected tree, naming the failed `:rule`: canonical-row production\n+   must not silently drop a frontend's coverage claim. The claim is\n+   checked root-relatively — admission origins belong to the admitting\n+   expander, not to this projection. A member carrying no markers\n+   makes no claim and passes; the executed tree's table is finalized\n+   after expansion, over the final rows. Answers true when the member\n+   claimed coverage (it passed the check), false when it carried no\n+   markers — one verdict per member, so the selected member's own\n+   verdict, never a sibling's, decides whether the expander finalizes\n+   its side table.\"\n+  [ast tree]\n+  (let [marked (marked-call-sites ast)]\n+    (if (seq marked)\n+      (do (doseq [[path value] marked]\n+            (when (not= 1 value)\n+              (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported call-site marker version\"\n+                              {:rule :yang/call-site-unsupported-version,\n+                               :path path, :value value}))))\n+          (let [eligible (into #{} (map second) (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n+                claimed (into #{} (map first) marked)]\n+            (when (not= eligible claimed)\n+              (throw (ex-info \"Call-site markers do not cover the projected tree\"\n+                              {:rule :yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage,\n+                               :missing (vec (sort-by pr-str\n+                                                      (remove claimed eligible))),\n+                               :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str\n+                                                    (remove eligible claimed)))}))))\n+          true)\n+      false)))\n+\n+\n (defn program-batch\n   \"Encode frontend output as the expander's input batch (§2.1):\n-   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows]`.\n-   Each member — a map AST or a `:yin/*` datom batch — projects to one tree\n-   packet; `run-index` selects the one that becomes the program. Harvest\n-   rows name every `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` occurrence in source\n-   declaration order, member by member; declaration rows name those whose\n-   lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`. No syntax object crosses: every\n-   code field is canonical rows.\"\n+   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows\n+   call-site-claims]` — the trailing element present only when some\n+   member claimed call-site (C1) coverage, holding one boolean verdict\n+   per member, so every unclaimed batch keeps the five-element shape.\n+   Each member — a map AST or a `:yin/*` datom batch\n+   — projects to one tree packet; `run-index` selects the one that\n+   becomes the program. Harvest rows name every `(yin/def\n+   <literal-symbol> value)` occurrence in source declaration order,\n+   member by member; declaration rows name those whose lambda the\n+   frontend flagged `:macro?`. No syntax object crosses: every code\n+   field is canonical rows. A member whose frontend markers claim\n+   call-site (C1) coverage is checked against its projected tree before\n+   the batch is formed (`check-call-site-claim!`): the markers drop out\n+   of the rows, but never silently — a broken claim refuses the batch,\n+   and the per-member claim verdicts travel with the batch, so the\n+   expander finalizes a member's executed tree's table when, and only\n+   when, that member's own verdict is a claim.\"\n   ([member] (program-batch [member] 0))\n   ([members run-index]\n    (let [asts (mapv member-ast members)\n-         trees (mapv (fn [ast]\n-                       (let [{:keys [root rows]} (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)]\n-                         [root (vec (vals rows))]))\n-                     asts)\n+         row-sets (mapv vm/ast->semantic-bytecode asts)\n+         trees (mapv (fn [{:keys [root rows]}] [root (vec (vals rows))])\n+                     row-sets)\n          occurrences (vec (mapcat (fn [j ast]\n                                     (map #(assoc % :tree j)\n                                          (definition-occurrences ast)))\n-                                  (range) asts))]\n-     [:yin.program/batch\n-      trees\n-      run-index\n-      (into [] (comp (filter :declared?)\n-                     (map (fn [{:keys [tree path]}] [:yin.macro/definition tree path])))\n-            occurrences)\n-      (into [] (map-indexed (fn [h {:keys [tree path]}]\n-                              [:yin.macro/harvest h tree path]))\n-            occurrences)])))\n+                                  (range) asts))\n+         ;; A frontend's C1 claim is enforced here, where its markers\n+         ;; would otherwise drop out of canonical-row production unread.\n+         ;; EVERY member is validated — `mapv` is eager, so a defect in\n+         ;; any member refuses the batch, however valid its siblings —\n+         ;; and the per-member verdicts ride with the batch: each\n+         ;; member's own verdict, never a sibling's, decides whether the\n+         ;; expander finalizes that member's side table.\n+         verdicts (mapv check-call-site-claim! asts row-sets)\n+         claims (when (some true? verdicts) verdicts)]\n+     (cond-> [:yin.program/batch\n+              trees\n+              run-index\n+              (into [] (comp (filter :declared?)\n+                             (map (fn [{:keys [tree path]}]\n+                                    [:yin.macro/definition tree path])))\n+                    occurrences)\n+              (into [] (map-indexed (fn [h {:keys [tree path]}]\n+                                      [:yin.macro/harvest h tree path]))\n+                    occurrences)]\n+       claims (conj claims)))))\n \n \n (defn ready?\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\nindex 8900fd54..44aacf0e 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\n@@ -738,11 +738,11 @@\n \n (def ^:private manifest-keys\n   \"The closed key set of a schema-1 manifest: every key of section 8.1's\n-   example, the index alone optional.\"\n+   example, the index and the call-site reference alone optional.\"\n   #{:yin.module/name :yin.module/schema :yin.module/contracts\n     :yin.module/tree :yin.module/derivations :yin.module/index\n     :yin.module/exports :yin.module/requires :yin.module/primitives\n-    :yin.module/footprint})\n+    :yin.module/footprint :yin.module/call-sites})\n \n \n (def ^:private derivation-formats\n@@ -785,7 +785,8 @@\n                   (when (or (not (contains? manifest k))\n                             (nil? (get manifest k)))\n                     (assoc (shape k) :missing true)))\n-                (disj manifest-keys :yin.module/index))\n+                (disj manifest-keys :yin.module/index\n+                      :yin.module/call-sites))\n           (when-not (symbol? (:yin.module/name manifest))\n             (shape :yin.module/name))\n           (when (vm/reserved-name? (:yin.module/name manifest))\n@@ -831,6 +832,16 @@\n                          (set? (get-in manifest\n                                        [:yin.module/footprint :effects])))\n             (shape :yin.module/footprint))\n+          ;; optional, and only when present checked: the C1 side-table\n+          ;; reference is exactly the table's and the reverse record's\n+          ;; Jing addresses (`yin.vm.linker.publish`)\n+          (let [call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\n+            (when (and (some? call-sites)\n+                       (not (and (map? call-sites)\n+                                 (= #{:table :record} (set (keys call-sites)))\n+                                 (address? (:table call-sites))\n+                                 (address? (:record call-sites)))))\n+              (shape :yin.module/call-sites)))\n           (some (fn [n]\n                   (when (vm/reserved-name? n)\n                     {:rule :reserved-name, :name n,\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\nindex 3b99b7ea..bfb8168e 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\n@@ -192,6 +192,43 @@\n (declare walk-module)\n \n \n+(defn- walk-call-sites\n+  \"Step 4b: the C1 side table and its reverse record the manifest\n+   references (`:yin.module/call-sites`, `yin.vm.linker.publish`), read\n+   and held to their own shape — the table is a vector of frontend-\n+   metadata rows, the record is version 1, names the manifest's own\n+   tree, and points at the referenced table. The origin is not\n+   recomputed or reconstructed here: each marker row carries its own\n+   occurrence origin (design §2.1), and the record persists the\n+   publication's admission identity, which the retriever reads from\n+   the record, never from the tree.\"\n+  [st manifest path]\n+  (if-some [call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\n+    (let [[st table] (read-blob st (:table call-sites) :call-site path)]\n+      (if (:stop st)\n+        st\n+        (let [[st record] (read-blob st (:record call-sites) :call-site path)]\n+          (cond\n+            (:stop st) st\n+\n+            (not (vector? table))\n+            (stop st (invalid (:table call-sites) :call-site path\n+                              :call-site-defect {:code :table-shape}))\n+\n+            (not= {:yang.call-site/version 1\n+                   :yang.call-site/root (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n+                   :yang.call-site/table (:table call-sites)}\n+                  (select-keys record\n+                               [:yang.call-site/version\n+                                :yang.call-site/root\n+                                :yang.call-site/table]))\n+            (stop st (invalid (:record call-sites) :call-site path\n+                              :call-site-defect {:code :record-shape}))\n+\n+            :else st))))\n+    st))\n+\n+\n (defn- walk-requires\n   \"Step 5: list every pin with derived eagerness, then descend only into\n    eager manifests not walked before. Deferred pins load at statement time.\"\n@@ -242,7 +279,8 @@\n                    (update :modules conj manifest-address)\n                    (walk-rows (:yin.module/tree manifest) path))\n             st (if (:stop st) st (walk-records st manifest path))\n-            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-images st manifest path))]\n+            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-images st manifest path))\n+            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-call-sites st manifest path))]\n         (if (:stop st)\n           st\n           (walk-requires st manifest-address manifest path depth))))))\n@@ -262,11 +300,13 @@\n      {:yin.link.closure/outcome :invalid\n       :address a :role role :path [...] :defect {:code c :detail d}}\n \n-   `role` is `:manifest`, `:row`, `:record`, `:image` or `:require`;\n+   `role` is `:manifest`, `:row`, `:record`, `:image`, `:call-site` or\n+   `:require`;\n    `path` the manifest addresses from the root to the module the blob\n    belongs to.  `:code` is one of `:address-mismatch`, `:manifest-defect`,\n    `:row-defect`, `:record-defect`, `:derivation-mismatch`,\n-   `:index-entry-missing`, `:identity-mismatch`, `:parts-limit`.\"\n+   `:index-entry-missing`, `:identity-mismatch`, `:call-site-defect`,\n+   `:parts-limit`.\"\n   ([handle manifest-address] (walk handle manifest-address nil))\n   ([handle manifest-address opts]\n    (let [bounds (into linker/default-bounds\n(deftest publisher-scope-admission-identity-test\n  (testing \"two independent publisher scopes producing identical\n            specifications still yield distinct admission identities\n            (design §2.1): the admission token is drawn from the\n            caller-owned scope object — no counter lives in the\n            publisher namespace, so two fresh publisher processes (or\n            restarts of one) publishing the same specification never\n            unknowingly share or split one admission identity\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (inc x)) (f 2)])\n          spec {:name 'scoped-twin\n                :ast ast\n                :exports #{'f}\n                :requires {}\n                :primitives {'inc {:yin.k/profile :yin.k/pure\n                                   :yin.k/effects #{}}}}\n          ;; two independent publisher processes: two stores, two scopes\n          store-a (mem/create-content-mem)\n          store-b (mem/create-content-mem)\n          scope-a (publish/admission-scope \"publisher-a\")\n          scope-b (publish/admission-scope \"publisher-b\")\n          via-a (publish/publish-module!\n                  store-a spec {:yin.link.publish/scope scope-a})\n          via-b (publish/publish-module!\n                  store-b spec {:yin.link.publish/scope scope-b})]\n      (is (some? (:address via-a)))\n      (is (some? (:address via-b)))\n      (is (= (get-in via-a [:call-sites :root])\n             (get-in via-b [:call-sites :root]))\n          \"the published trees are content-identical\")\n      (is (not= (get-in via-a [:call-sites :origin])\n                (get-in via-b [:call-sites :origin]))\n          \"identical specs, independent scopes: distinct admissions\")\n      (doseq [[label result store]\n              [[\"scope-a\" via-a store-a] [\"scope-b\" via-b store-b]]]\n        (let [{:keys [tree origin rows]}\n              (publish/published-call-site-table store (:address result))]\n          (is (some? rows) (str label \" table retrieves\"))\n          (is (= (eligible-under tree origin) (marked rows)))\n          (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n                       tree rows origin {:declared? true}))))))))\n\n(defn- correspondences\n  \"Every expansion correspondence the log recorded.\"\n  [log]\n  (map #(nth % 11) (nth log 1)))\n\n\n(deftest p1-packet-provenance-test\n  (testing \"packet reassembly retains the incoming origin (P1-1)\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n                '[(defmacro repack [x]\n                    (conj [] (first x) (first (rest x))))\n                  (repack (+ 1 2))])\n          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]]\n      (is (= :ok status))\n      (is (contains? (set (correspondences log))\n                     {[] [:retained admission]})\n          \"the reassembled packet records the incoming origin as\n           retained, never fabricated construction\")\n      (is (= #{admission} (row-origins frontend-metadata))\n          \"the retained application keeps its source origin\")\n      (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n                   final frontend-metadata admission\n                   {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))))\n  (testing \"a reassembled packet inserted as a child retains its origin (P1-1)\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n                '[(defmacro repack-call [x]\n                    (yin/application (yin/variable 'f)\n                                     [(conj [] (first x)\n                                            (first (rest x)))]))\n                  (defn f [y] y)\n                  (repack-call (+ 1 2))])\n          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n          event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))]\n      (is (= :ok status))\n      (is (contains? (set (correspondences log))\n                     {[] :constructed, [[3 0]] [:retained admission]})\n          \"the built call is constructed; the reassembled child keeps\n           its incoming origin\")\n      (is (contains? (row-origins frontend-metadata) admission))\n      (is (some (fn [o]\n                  (and (expansion-origin? o)\n                       (contains? event-addrs (second o))))\n                (row-origins frontend-metadata))\n          \"the built call names its recorded expansion event\")\n      (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n                   final frontend-metadata admission\n                   {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))))\n  (testing \"equal-content operands: reassembly recovers its own occurrence (P1-1)\"\n    ;; `a` and `b` hold identical row objects (one shared index), but\n    ;; `a` retains the source admission while `b` belongs to the\n    ;; `feed` expansion; recovering `a`'s origin for `b` is the\n    ;; ambiguous row-level match this pin refuses.\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n                '[(defmacro pick-second [a b]\n                    (conj [] (first b) (first (rest b))))\n                  (defmacro feed [x]\n                    (yin/application (yin/variable 'pick-second)\n                      [x (yin/application (yin/variable 'f)\n                                           [(yin/literal 1)])]))\n                  (defn f [y] y)\n                  (feed (f 1))])\n          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n          event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n          corrs (correspondences log)]\n      (is (= :ok status))\n      (is (some (fn [corr]\n                  (let [o (get corr [])]\n                    (and (vector? o) (= :retained (first o))\n                         (expansion-origin? (second o))\n                         (contains? event-addrs (second (second o))))))\n                corrs)\n          \"reassembling b recovers the feed-expansion origin\")\n      (is (not (contains? (set corrs) {[] [:retained admission]}))\n          \"never the other occurrence's source admission\")\n      (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n                   final frontend-metadata admission\n                   {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))))\n  (testing \"a packet entering a literal slot encodes cleanly (P1-2)\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n                '[(defmacro packet-data [x] (yin/literal x))\n                  (packet-data (+ 1 2))])\n          {:keys [result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n          {:keys [status tree]} result\n          payload (some (fn [row]\n                          (when (and (= :literal (nth row 1))\n                                     (vector? (nth row 2)))\n                            (nth row 2)))\n                        (second tree))]\n      (is (= :ok status)\n          \"private tracking metadata never reaches the encoder\")\n      (is (some? payload) \"the operand survives as literal data\")\n      (is (not (contains? (or (meta payload) {})\n                          :yin.vm.macro/origin-of))\n          \"only the private tracking entry is removed\")\n      (is (nil? (macro/valid-tree? tree))))))\n\n\n(deftest publisher-scope-id-identity-test\n  (testing \"scope ids keep their full identity: a keyword's namespace\n            and a string's type are part of the id, so :a/publisher,\n            :b/publisher and \\\"publisher\\\" mint distinct tokens even at\n            the same ordinal\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (inc x)) (f 2)])\n          spec {:name 'scoped-ids\n                :ast ast\n                :exports #{'f}\n                :requires {}\n                :primitives {'inc {:yin.k/profile :yin.k/pure\n                                   :yin.k/effects #{}}}}\n          publish-with-scope\n          (fn [id]\n            (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)]\n              [store (publish/publish-module!\n                       store spec {:yin.link.publish/scope\n                                   (publish/admission-scope id)})]))\n          [_ res-a] (publish-with-scope :a/publisher)\n          [_ res-b] (publish-with-scope :b/publisher)\n          [_ res-s] (publish-with-scope \"publisher\")]\n      (is (not= (get-in res-a [:call-sites :origin])\n                (get-in res-b [:call-sites :origin]))\n          \":a/publisher and :b/publisher stay distinct (namespace kept)\")\n      (is (not= (get-in res-a [:call-sites :origin])\n                (get-in res-s [:call-sites :origin]))\n          \"the keyword and the string of the same name stay distinct\"))))","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
