{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '150,390p' /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   and the content address of its compiled tree — never from hidden\n   mutable state. Two publications of the same specification therefore\n   answer the same admission identity (an idempotent re-publication is\n   the same recorded admission), and distinct specifications never\n   share one, in this or any other publisher process. A composition\n   that admits the same specification more than once as separate\n   admissions passes an `:yin.link.publish/scope` (or an explicit\n   `:yin.link.publish/admission`) so the admissions stay distinct.\"\n  [{:keys [name]} tree]\n  (keyword \"yin.vm.linker.publish.publication\"\n           (str name \"::\" (:root tree))))\n\n(defn- publication-origin\n  \"The occurrence origin of the publication admission `token` names:\n   the publisher's own medium, the explicit admission token, member 0.\n   `token` is the publication's admission identity — the\n   `:yin.link.publish/admission` option when the composition pins one,\n   the `:yin.link.publish/scope` option's next drawn token when the\n   composition scopes the publisher, otherwise the token derived from\n   the publication specification's own durable identity. The origin is\n   an admission event's identity, not a function of the tree's content\n   alone: it is persisted in the side record at publication time and\n   retrieved from that record; nothing ever reconstructs it from the\n   root.\"\n  [token]\n  [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0])\n\n\n(defn- claims-call-sites?\n  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 key anywhere. A hit inside a\n   literal payload is data, not a claim: extraction then finds no\n   markers and the module publishes unannotated, as it should.\"\n  [ast]\n  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn- call-site-claim\n  \"The C1 claim `ast` makes over its canonical `tree`: nil when it\n   carries no markers; `{:origin o :rows [...]}` in printed-row order\n   when the extracted markers exactly cover the tree's eligible\n   application occurrences; `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` when they\n   do not; `{:unsupported-version v :path p}` when a marker's value is\n   not version 1 — a claim rejection, never a silent acceptance of a\n   table a retriever would read as version 1.\"\n  [ast tree admission]\n  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n    (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\n          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n                            (:frontend-metadata\n                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n          eligible (into #{}\n                         (map (fn [[r p]] [origin r p]))\n                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n          marked (into #{}\n                       (map (fn [[o r p _ _]] [o r p]))\n                       extracted)]\n      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\n                                   (let [v (nth row 4)]\n                                     (when (not (and (integer? v) (= 1 v)))\n                                       [v (subvec row 0 3)])))\n                                 extracted)]\n            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\n          (if (= eligible marked)\n            {:origin origin, :rows (vec (sort-by pr-str extracted))}\n            {:missing (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove marked eligible))),\n             :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove eligible marked)))})))))\n\n\n(defn link-local\n  \"Link `format`'s image through the manifest `address` over `handle`'s\n   own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\n   composition does (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1): a fresh local runtime per\n   call, so no request reaches any peer.  `opts` overrides the link\n   options; its `:bounds` are the runtime's composition bounds (section\n   4.2 step 2), every one left out taking `linker/default-bounds`.\"\n  ([handle address format] (link-local handle address format nil))\n  ([handle address format opts]\n   (linker/link-manifest\n     (linker/local-runtime\n       handle {:formats (into {} (map (fn [f] [(:format f) f]))\n                              (conj code-formats linker/manifest-format\n                                    linker/record-format))\n               :bounds (:bounds opts)})\n     address (:format format) {:primitives vm/primitives}\n     (merge {:contract (:contract format)\n             :derivation :verifying\n             :defer-discharge true}\n            (dissoc opts :bounds)))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-closure!\n  \"`publish-module!` under the composition bounds of `opts`.\"\n  [handle {:keys [name ast exports requires primitives] :as spec} opts]\n  (let [undefined (first (remove (definitions ast) exports))\n        tree (when-not undefined\n               (try (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n                      (refusal :yin.link.publish/malformed-tree {}))))\n        defect (when (and tree (not= :refused (:status tree)))\n                 (vm/validate-rows tree))\n        ;; each pinned closure is walked before anything is written; an\n        ;; absent pinned manifest is the footprint's missing-requirement\n        requirement\n        (when (and tree (not defect) (not= :refused (:status tree)))\n          (some (fn [[n address]]\n                  (let [w (closure/walk handle address opts)]\n                    (case (:yin.link.closure/outcome w)\n                      :complete nil\n                      :invalid (refusal :yin.link.publish/invalid-requirement\n                                        {:name n})\n                      :missing (when (not= address (:address w))\n                                 (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-requirement\n                                          {:name n :walk w})))))\n                (sort-by (fn [[n _]] (str n)) requires)))\n        fp (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\n                      (not= :refused (:status tree)))\n             (footprint handle (assoc spec :tree tree)))\n        ;; a C1 claim is validated before anything is written: a module\n        ;; whose markers do not cover its tree is never published as\n        ;; though it did. One publication is one admission event\n        ;; (design §2.1): the admission identity is pinned explicitly by\n        ;; the composition when it supplies `:yin.link.publish/admission`,\n        ;; drawn from the composition's own scope object when it supplies\n        ;; `:yin.link.publish/scope`, and otherwise derived from the\n        ;; specification's own durable identity — no counter lives in\n        ;; this namespace. Either way it is persisted in the side record\n        ;; and retrieved from there\n        admission (or (:yin.link.publish/admission opts)\n                      (when-let [scope (:yin.link.publish/scope opts)]\n                        (scope-admission-token scope))\n                      (when tree (spec-admission-token spec tree)))\n        claim (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\n                         (not= :refused (:status tree))\n                         (not= :refused (:status fp)))\n                (call-site-claim ast tree admission))]\n    (cond\n      undefined\n      (refusal :yin.link.publish/undefined-export {:export undefined})\n\n      (= :refused (:status tree)) tree\n\n      defect\n      (refusal :yin.link.publish/malformed-tree {:defect defect})\n\n      requirement requirement\n\n      (= :refused (:status fp)) fp\n\n      ;; dispatch on the key's PRESENCE, not its truthiness: a marker\n      ;; whose value is present but not the integer 1 — nil or false\n      ;; included — carries :unsupported-version nil/false, and its\n      ;; reason is the unsupported version, never incomplete coverage\n      (and claim (contains? claim :unsupported-version))\n      (refusal :yin.link.publish/unsupported-call-site-version claim)\n\n      (and claim (not (:rows claim)))\n      (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage claim)\n\n      :else\n      (let [tree-address (vm/materialize-tree! handle tree)\n            sem-vector (:vector (linearize/project-rows tree))\n            sem (code/materialize-vector! handle sem-vector)\n            h-image (:image (derive/stack-image sem-vector))\n            r-image (derive/register-image sem-vector)\n            h (dcode/image-hash h-image)\n            r (rcode/register-hash r-image)\n            h-address (jing/materialize! handle h-image)\n            r-address (jing/materialize! handle r-image)\n            mint (fn [input output profile]\n                   (jing/materialize!\n                     handle\n                     (assoc (ledger/derive-record input output)\n                            :yin.ledger/profile profile)))\n            ;; the C1 side table and its reverse record, materialized\n            ;; BEFORE the manifest so the manifest can reference them:\n            ;; the module closure follows manifest references, so only a\n            ;; referenced table travels with the module through transfer\n            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n                         (let [table (jing/materialize! handle (:rows claim))\n                               record {:yang.call-site/version 1\n                                       :yang.call-site/root tree-address\n                                       :yang.call-site/origin (:origin claim)\n                                       :yang.call-site/table table}]\n                           {:record (jing/materialize! handle record)\n                            :table table\n                            :origin (:origin claim)\n                            :root (:root tree)}))\n            manifest (cond-> {:yin.module/name name\n                              :yin.module/schema linker/manifest-schema\n                              :yin.module/contracts\n                              {:yin.ast/code vm/ast-contract\n                               :yin.semantic/code vm/semantic-contract\n                               :yin.debruijn.code vm/stack-contract\n                               :yin.debruijn.register vm/register-contract}\n                              :yin.module/tree tree-address\n                              :yin.module/derivations\n                              {:yin.semantic/code (mint tree-address sem ledger/lowering-profile)\n                               :yin.debruijn.code\n                               (mint sem h linker/stack-lowering-profile)\n                               :yin.debruijn.register\n                               (mint sem r linker/register-lowering-profile)}\n                              :yin.module/index {:yin.debruijn.code h-address\n                                                 :yin.debruijn.register r-address}\n                              :yin.module/exports (set exports)\n                              :yin.module/requires (or requires {})\n                              :yin.module/primitives\n                              (into {} (map (fn [[n p]] [n (:yin.k/profile p)])\n                                            primitives))\n                              :yin.module/footprint fp}\n                       call-sites (assoc :yin.module/call-sites\n                                         {:table (:table call-sites)\n                                          :record (:record call-sites)}))\n            address (jing/materialize! handle manifest)\n            walked (closure/walk handle address opts)]\n        (if (not= :complete (:yin.link.closure/outcome walked))\n          (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-closure\n                   {:address address :walk walked})\n          (let [links (into {}\n                            (map (fn [f]\n                                   [(:format f)\n                                    (link-local handle address f\n                                                (select-keys opts\n                                                             [:bounds]))]))\n                            code-formats)]\n            (cond-> {:address address :manifest manifest\n                     :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n                                  :yin.debruijn.code sem\n                                  :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n                     :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h\n                                 :yin.debruijn.register r}\n                     :links links}\n              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n\n\n(defn publish-module!\n  \"Mint all four code formats, derivation records, and one schema-1 manifest.\n   `opts` `{:bounds {...}}` are the composition bounds (section 4.2 step\n   2) of every closure walk and local link the publication runs, every\n   bound left out taking `linker/default-bounds`. `opts` may also pin\n   the publication's admission identity explicitly\n   (`:yin.link.publish/admission`) or scope it — a scope object from\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '90,130p' /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc; nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '605,785p'; nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '875,945p'; rg -n \\\"'assoc|'conj|'rest|defn.*assoc\\\" /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '90,130p' /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc; nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '605,785p'; nl -ba /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '875,945p'; rg -n \\\"'assoc|'conj|'rest|defn.*assoc\\\" /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- reachable\n  \"Addresses reachable from `root` through `index`, first-encounter preorder\n   in grammar order. Assumes the index is closed and acyclic.\"\n  [index root]\n  (loop [stack (list root)\n         seen #{}\n         order []]\n    (if-let [a (first stack)]\n      (if (contains? seen a)\n        (recur (rest stack) seen order)\n        (recur (reduce conj (rest stack) (reverse (map second (child-places (get index a)))))\n               (conj seen a)\n               (conj order a)))\n      order)))\n\n\n(defn- packet-of\n  \"The self-contained tree packet `[root rows]` rooted at `root` (§1.2). Row\n   order is preorder, which is deterministic but carries no meaning.\"\n  [index root]\n  [root (mapv #(get index %) (reachable index root))])\n\n\n(defn tree-packet\n  \"Convert a projected row set `{:root id :rows {id row}}` (the shape\n   `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns) to a tree packet `[root rows]`.\"\n  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n  (packet-of rows root))\n\n\n(defn packet->row-set\n  \"Convert a canonical tree packet to `{:root id :rows {id row}}`, the shape\n   the evaluator loaders take.\"\n  [[root rows]]\n  {:root root, :rows (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) rows)})\n\n\n(defn ast->packet\n  \"Project a map AST to its canonical tree packet.\"\n  [ast]\n  (tree-packet (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n   605\t   table, a row, or an event it does not belong to.\"\n   606\t  [:expansion ::pending])\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- with-origin-of\n   610\t  \"Tag packet `p` with `f`, its construction origin function: `(f rel)`\n   611\t   answers the origin of the occurrence at `rel`, a path relative to\n   612\t   `p`'s root — the pending expansion origin for a node the macro's\n   613\t   code constructed, or, below a child coordinate that retains a\n   614\t   passed-through packet, that packet's own origin function. The\n   615\t   function rides the packet's metadata, so it is content-addressing\n   616\t   invisible and never leaks into a final tree.\"\n   617\t  [p f]\n   618\t  (vary-meta p assoc ::origin-of f))\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\t(defn- origin-of-fn\n   622\t  \"The construction origin function packet `p` carries, or nil.\"\n   623\t  [p]\n   624\t  (::origin-of (meta p)))\n   625\t\n   626\t\n   627\t(def ^:private tracking-meta-keys\n   628\t  \"The private provenance entries the expander rides on packet values.\n   629\t   They are host functions, so they must never enter a hashed or\n   630\t   validated data slot (P1-2); every other metadata entry is the\n   631\t   caller's legitimate data and is preserved.\"\n   632\t  #{::origin-of})\n   633\t\n   634\t\n   635\t(defn- strip-tracking\n   636\t  \"Remove only the private tracking entries, recursively, from `x`:\n   637\t   every collection element, map key and value, and every metadata map\n   638\t   (including metadata on metadata) is visited, so a packet nested at\n   639\t   any depth inside a literal payload loses its host-function origin\n   640\t   while legitimate user metadata survives untouched.\"\n   641\t  [x]\n   642\t  (let [x' (cond (record? x) x\n   643\t                 (map? x) (into (empty x)\n   644\t                                (map (fn [[k v]]\n   645\t                                       [(strip-tracking k)\n   646\t                                        (strip-tracking v)]))\n   647\t                                x)\n   648\t                 (set? x) (into (empty x) (map strip-tracking) x)\n   649\t                 (vector? x) (mapv strip-tracking x)\n   650\t                 (sequential? x) (with-meta\n   651\t                                   (apply list (map strip-tracking x))\n   652\t                                   nil)\n   653\t                 :else x)\n   654\t        m (meta x)]\n   655\t    (if m\n   656\t      (let [m' (strip-tracking\n   657\t                 (apply dissoc m tracking-meta-keys))]\n   658\t        (with-meta x' (when-not (and (empty? m') (nil? (meta m'))) m')))\n   659\t      x')))\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\t(defn- packet-has-application?\n   663\t  \"True when packet `p` contains an `:application` occurrence, the only\n   664\t   occurrences whose provenance a correspondence ever reads.\"\n   665\t  [p]\n   666\t  (boolean (and (packet? p)\n   667\t                (some #(= :application (row-tag %)) (second p)))))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t(defn- register-lineage!\n   671\t  \"Record packet `p` in the invocation `lineage` (an atom of entries)\n   672\t   under the identity of its rows vector. Host decomposition\n   673\t   (`first`/`rest`/`get`) hands that very object to reassembly, so the\n   674\t   entry is how a rebuilt packet proves it is this packet retained,\n   675\t   never a content twin built anew. Returns `p`.\"\n   676\t  [lineage p]\n   677\t  (when (and lineage (packet? p) (origin-of-fn p))\n   678\t    (when-not (some #(identical? (second p) (:rows %)) @lineage)\n   679\t      (swap! lineage conj {:root (first p), :rows (second p),\n   680\t                           :fn (origin-of-fn p)})))\n   681\t  p)\n   682\t\n   683\t\n   684\t(defn- lineage-origin-for\n   685\t  \"The retained origin function for candidate packet `c`, or nil when\n   686\t   no registered packet unambiguously accounts for it. Content\n   687\t   equality alone never suffices — a freshly built twin holds equal\n   688\t   but distinct row objects and recovers nothing here (ruling U1).\n   689\t\n   690\t   Exact container lineage is preferred: a registered packet whose\n   691\t   rows vector is the very object `c` carries (host decomposition\n   692\t   hands that object to reassembly) is occurrence-specific, so it\n   693\t   wins over any row-level match. Row-level recovery — the root\n   694\t   matches and every row is `identical?` to a registered packet's\n   695\t   row in order — is taken only when exactly one distinct origin\n   696\t   function matches: distinct occurrences of identical content share\n   697\t   row objects (`packet-of` retrieves them from one index), so a\n   698\t   first-match pick among ambiguous row-level candidates would\n   699\t   attach another occurrence's origin. Ambiguity is refused (nil),\n   700\t   which downstream reads as missing provenance, never as a guess.\"\n   701\t  [lineage c]\n   702\t  (when (and lineage (packet? c) (nil? (origin-of-fn c)))\n   703\t    (let [entries (filter #(= (:root %) (first c)) @lineage)\n   704\t          rows (second c)\n   705\t          only-fn (fn [es]\n   706\t                    (let [fns (distinct (map :fn es))]\n   707\t                      (when (= 1 (count fns)) (first fns))))\n   708\t          exact (filter #(identical? (:rows %) rows) entries)]\n   709\t      (if (seq exact)\n   710\t        (only-fn exact)\n   711\t        (only-fn (filter #(and (= (count (:rows %)) (count rows))\n   712\t                               (every? true?\n   713\t                                       (map identical? (:rows %) rows)))\n   714\t                         entries))))))\n   715\t\n   716\t\n   717\t(def ^:private missing-provenance-origin\n   718\t  \"The origin an unaccounted child answers below its coordinate: no\n   719\t   sanctioned operation threaded provenance to it, so nothing may\n   720\t   relabel its occurrences as this expansion's construction (P1-1).\n   721\t   `output-correspondence` carries the marker through and\n   722\t   `expand-call` refuses the output as `:missing-provenance`; the\n   723\t   marker never reaches a table, a row, or an event.\"\n   724\t  [:expansion ::missing])\n   725\t\n   726\t\n   727\t(defn- constructed-origin-fn\n   728\t  \"The origin function of a packet the prelude constructed: its root\n   729\t   occurrence carries the pending expansion origin; a relative path\n   730\t   below a child coordinate delegates to the packet passed for that\n   731\t   child — a spliced operand retains its own incoming origin, however\n   732\t   the macro's code embedded it. `recover` answers a child packet's\n   733\t   retained origin function when the packet itself carries none (it\n   734\t   was rebuilt by decomposition/reassembly); a child neither source\n   735\t   accounts for answers `missing-provenance-origin` below its\n   736\t   coordinate, which the expander refuses rather than reads as\n   737\t   construction.\"\n   738\t  ([coord-children] (constructed-origin-fn coord-children (fn [_] nil)))\n   739\t  ([coord-children recover]\n   740\t   (fn [rel]\n   741\t     (if (empty? rel)\n   742\t       pending-expansion-origin\n   743\t       (if-some [child (get coord-children (first rel))]\n   744\t         (if-some [f (or (origin-of-fn child) (recover child))]\n   745\t           (f (subvec rel 1))\n   746\t           missing-provenance-origin)\n   747\t         pending-expansion-origin)))))\n   748\t\n   749\t\n   750\t(defn- construct\n   751\t  \"Intern `body` over the rows of its child `packets`; a closed packet.\n   752\t   Every node interned here is CONSTRUCTED by the expansion's code\n   753\t   (ruling U1), so the result packet carries the construction origin\n   754\t   function and the output's per-occurrence origins are read from this\n   755\t   construction history — never inferred by comparing content\n   756\t   addresses: a constructed node whose content equals a retained\n   757\t   node's stays distinct, because its origin answers through this\n   758\t   function and not through its address.\n   759\t\n   760\t   Values entering `:data`/`:key` slots are stripped of private\n   761\t   tracking metadata first (P1-2), before hashing and validation.\n   762\t   Missing child provenance never proves construction (P1-1): the\n   763\t   result's origin function answers the missing marker below an\n   764\t   unaccounted child and the expander refuses such an output.\"\n   765\t  ([body packets] (construct body packets nil))\n   766\t  ([body packets lineage]\n   767\t   (let [recover (fn [child] (lineage-origin-for lineage child))]\n   768\t     (let [tag (first body)\n   769\t           slots (get working-grammar tag)\n   770\t           body (if (and slots (= (count slots) (count (rest body))))\n   771\t                  (into [tag]\n   772\t                        (map (fn [[_ kind] v]\n   773\t                               (if (contains? #{:data :key} kind)\n   774\t                                 (strip-tracking v)\n   775\t                                 v))\n   776\t                             slots\n   777\t                             (rest body)))\n   778\t                  body)\n   779\t           index (merge-packets packets)\n   780\t           [index a] (intern-body index body)\n   781\t           coord-children (into {}\n   782\t                                (map (fn [[place p]] [(first place) p]))\n   783\t                                (map vector (child-places (get index a)) packets))]\n   784\t       (with-origin-of (packet-of index a)\n   785\t         (constructed-origin-fn coord-children recover))))))\n   875\t\n   876\t   The collection primitives are provenance-aware within one invocation\n   877\t   (P1-1): decomposing a packet (`first`/`rest`/`get`) registers its\n   878\t   lineage, and reassembling one (`conj`/`assoc`/`vec`) reattaches the\n   879\t   retained origin function when the rebuilt packet holds the very row\n   880\t   objects it was decomposed from. A packet rebuilt any other way\n   881\t   carries no provenance and is refused downstream rather than\n   882\t   relabelled as construction.\"\n   883